<article class="env-lemma" id="6EE0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6EE0">Lemma <span data-tag="6EE0">5.3.5.7</span>.</a> Let $\calD $ be an $\infty $-category $($not necessarily small$)$. There exists a fully faithful functor $i: \calD \rightarrow \calD '$ with the following properties: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The $\infty $-category $\calD '$ admits small colimits. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
A small diagram $K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calD $ is a colimit if and only if the composite map $K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calD '$ is a colimit. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\calD ' = \Fun ( \calD , \widehat{\SSet })^{op}$, and let $i$ be the opposite of the Yoneda embedding. Then $(1)$ follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/4396" data-tag="4396">5.1.2.2</a> and $(2)$ from Proposition <a href="/tag/DA1B" data-tag="DA1B">5.1.3.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>